 length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 09:57:41 +0100</pubDate></item><item><title>(Research) C. Brandon Ogbunu argues risk aversion stifles scientific innovation</title><link>https://undark.org/2026/06/04/opinion-risk-aversion-innovation/</link><description>&lt;b&gt;Source:&lt;/b&gt; Undark Magazine&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src='https://undark.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/GettyImages-1754587081_crop.jpg' alt='thumbnail' style='max-width:100%; border-radius:8px;'/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;C. Brandon Ogbunu argues that excessive risk aversion within the scientific enterprise hinders innovation. He contends that true scientific advancement requires a willingness to critically reflect on and dramatically overhaul existing processes and incentives that currently discourage bold, unconventional research. This perspective is relevant for UK/EU academics, policymakers, and funding bodies seeking to foster scientific progress and innovation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;small&gt;&lt;b&gt;How did this land?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href='https://redirect-service-73lh.onrender.com/signal?item=https%3A//undark.org/2026/06/04/opinion-risk-aversion-innovation/&amp;signal=3&amp;source=Undark%20Magazine&amp;type=rss&amp;context=amazingly_hopeful%20%7C%20Topic%3A%20C.%20Brandon%20Ogbunu%20argues%20risk%20aversion%20stifles%20scientific%20innovation&amp;dest=https%3A//maxmrry.github.io/curious-rabbit-hole-bot/&amp;token=9412ce3ed98e5434694fdbb1057a07ce58d5928e92b5cb466c9677cb0e6bd128' style='text-decoration:none;'&gt;🥇✅ Wow, I Feel Positive, Inspired, Impressed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href='https://redirect-service-73lh.onrender.com/signal?item=https%3A//undark.org/2026/06/04/opinion-risk-aversion-innovation/&amp;signal=2&amp;source=Undark%20Magazine&amp;type=rss&amp;context=pretty_positive%20%7C%20Topic%3A%20C.%20Brandon%20Ogbunu%20argues%20risk%20aversion%20stifles%20scientific%20innovation&amp;dest=https%3A//maxmrry.github.io/curious-rabbit-hole-bot/&amp;